<%# The rest of a table row, for the width where the table is one column.

    Below `lg` every table in this app shows its first column and nothing else: the other cells are
    `hidden lg:table-cell`, and their values come back here as labelled lines inside the primary cell.
    That is the trading floor's treatment, generalised - it was the only table in the app that fitted
    375px, because it was the only one that collapsed instead of scrolling. Nine tables scrolled between
    196px and 685px sideways, which on a phone means the data is behind a gesture nobody is told about.

    A description list, because a label and a value is what a `<dl>` is for, and because `sr-only` labels
    would leave a column of bare values with nothing saying which is which. The `<th>`s stay with their
    columns and disappear with them: a header for a column nobody can see names nothing.

    Values may be pre-rendered markup - a badge, a link, an em dash for absent - so they arrive already
    escaped or already safe from the caller.

    Locals:
      fields  - array of [label, value] pairs, in the order the columns appear
      actions - optional pre-rendered row actions, placed after the fields %>
<% fields = local_assigns[:fields] || [] %>

<% if fields.any? %>
  <dl class="mt-2 space-y-1 lg:hidden">
    <% fields.each do |label, value| %>
      <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between gap-3">
        <dt class="shrink-0 text-xs text-slate-600"><%= label %></dt>
        <dd class="min-w-0 text-right text-sm text-slate-900"><%= value %></dd>
      </div>
    <% end %>
  </dl>
<% end %>

<%# Row actions sit after the data, not before it: below lg they are the last thing in the row, which is
    where they are at lg too. `flex-wrap` because three labelled ghosts are ~250px and the cell is ~300px
    minus its padding, so the third can need a second line. %>
<% if local_assigns[:actions].present? %>
  <%# The testid is how a test tells a row *action* from any other link in the row. Since the record's
      name became a link in its own right, `tbody tr a` no longer means "a row action" - and the test
      that measures their height and icons was reading the 17px name link as one. %>
  <div class="mt-3 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-1 lg:hidden"
       data-testid="stacked-row-actions"><%= actions %></div>
<% end %>
